%description:

Tcp.dsackEnabled:on -- the receiver reports a duplicate segment by a D-SACK block.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "report duplicate segments by D-SACK blocks (RFC 2883), when SACK is in
use". The default is the value of sackSupport.

The classes: on (true), off (false). The code: a duplicate segment sets the D-SACK report
when SACK is in use and D-SACK is on (TcpConnection::processSegment1stThru8th()), and the
next SACK option starts with that block (TcpConnection::addSacks()). This test separates
"on" from "off": with "off", the ACK has no D-SACK block.

Host under test: host2, the receiver; both hosts support SACK (the default). Peer: host1
sends one segment of 1000 bytes, and the tap delivers a copy of it 2 ms later. Observation:
level 1, the first ACK of host2 after the copy: its first SACK block reports data below the
cumulative ACK.

%# parameter: Tcp.dsackEnabled
%# class: on
%# value: true
%# key: *.host2.tcp.dsackEnabled
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpMutations.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpDsackEnabledOn")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1)
                     .duplicate(0.002)
                     .describe("the data segment, and a copy of it 2 ms later"))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
                  .describe("the data segment at host2")
                  .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
                  .describe("the copy at host2")
                  .within(0.01))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.ackBit == true")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) { return hasDsackBlock(context.event.packet); })
                  .describe("the ACK of the copy, with a D-SACK block")
                  .within(0.01));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpDsackEnabledOn compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.dsackEnabled = true    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 1000B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpDsackEnabledOn: PASS
